  "raw_text": "303\n\nREGULAR VERBS / VERBOS REGULARES\n\nTo conjugate a regular verb, drop the “\naia\n” and add to the stem the ending as seen below.\n \n/\n\nPara conjugar un verbo regular, suelte el \"\naia\n\" y agregue a la raíz el final como se ve a continuación.\n\nRegular Verbs / Verbos Regulares\n\nBlack\n \nletters are root / Letras\n \nnegras\n \nson raíz\n\nGreen\n \nletters are conjugation / Letras\n \nverdes\n \nson conjugación\n\nAdding the letters that are\n \norange\n \nindicates that the subject who does the verb action is plural /\n\nAgregar las letras que son de color\n \nnaranja\n \nindica que el sujeto que realiza la acción verbal es plural\n\nUsing / Usando:\n \nLukaia\n \n–\n \nto think, to care\n \n/ pensar\n\nPresent\n \nI /\nPresente I\n\nPresent II /\nPresente II\n\nPast I /\nPasado I\n\nPast II /\nPasado II\n\nFuture I /\nFuturo I\n\nFuture II /\nFuturo II\n\nYang (1\nst\n/1\ner\n)\n \nLukuna\n \nLukisna\n \nLukatna\n \nLukri\n \nLukaisna\n \nLukamna\n\nMan (2\nnd\n/2\ndo\n)\n \nLukuma\n \nLukisma\n \nLukatma\n \nLukram\n \nLukaisma\n \nLukma\n\nWitin(3\nrd\n/3\ner\n),Yawan\n \nLukuya\n \nLukisa\n \nLukata\n \nLukan\n \nLukaisa\n \nLukbia\n\nYang nani (1\nst\n/1\ner\n)\n \nLuki\nbanhwuna\n\nLuki\nbanhwisna\n\nLuki\nbanhwatna\n\nLuki\nbanhwri\n\nLuki\nbanhwaisna\n\nLuki\nbanhwamna\n\nMan nani (2\nnd\n/2\ndo\n)\n \nLuki\nbanhwuma\n\nLuki\nbanhwisma\n\nLuki\nbanhwatma\n\nLuki\nbanhwram\n\nLuki\nbanhwaisma\n\nLuki\nbanhwma\n\nWitin nani (3\nrd\n/3\ner\n)\n \nLuki\nbanhwuya\n\nLuki\nbanhwisa\n\nLuki\nbanhwata\n\nLuki\nbanhwan\n\nLuki\nbanhwaisa\n\nLuki\nbanhwbia\n\nImperative\n/Imperativa\n:\n \nLuk\ns\n\nProhibitive\n/Prohibitiva\n:\n \nLuk\npara\n\nNegative\n/Negativa\n:\n \nLuk\nras\n\nPresent participle/ Participio presente:\n \nLuki",
